// Input-parser fixture: `ws(P)` at the ROOT, over a newline-terminated file.
//
// §7.5's `ws(parser)` splits on spaces or tabs — that names the separator, and
// a token contains no whitespace of any kind. The input this reads is an
// ordinary file, so it ends with `\n`; a repair that made the last token `3\n`
// and asked `int` to eat the terminator faulted here. Every other `ws` test in
// the tree deliberately omits the newline, which is how that got through.
//
// Reference state: PASSES at the pre-S20 base b2184c8, fails at 9458fd5. The
// defect was introduced and closed inside this branch — a regression fixture,
// not a gate for an audit finding.
fn main() -> Int {
    let v = read ws(int);
    var total = 0;
    for n in v {
        total = total + n;
    }
    total
}
